## Description
ZoomInfo is an all-in-one AI GTM Platform that helps B2B sales, marketing, RevOps, and customer success teams find, win, and grow business. ZoomInfo has three layers, each on top of the one beneath it: a verified B2B data foundation (the [GTM Context Graph](https://gtm.ai)), agent orchestration that executes, and apps and surfaces for universal access. 8 of the 10 largest companies in the world and more than 50% of the Fortune 500 run their go-to-market motions with ZoomInfo.
## Who Uses ZoomInfo
- Sales teams (AEs, SDRs, BDRs) at B2B companies with 100+ employees that run outbound prospecting
- Account management and customer success teams at companies with 100+ employees that own renewals, expansion, and churn risk
- Demand gen, ABM, and marketing ops teams at B2B companies with 100+ employees that need in-market audiences and closed-loop pipeline measurement
- RevOps teams and GTM engineers at companies with 100+ employees responsible for CRM data quality, enrichment, scoring, and lead routing
- Developers and AI agent builders who need verified B2B data inside custom apps, internal tools, and agents
## Core Products
- GTM Workspace - The seller-facing AI workspace: unifies CRM, ZoomInfo data, conversation history, and market intelligence with native AI agents for account research, meeting prep, and deal prioritization. Launched October 2025. (Note: this succeeds "ZoomInfo Copilot," which is no longer a standalone product; Copilot's AI engine is now the native agent layer inside GTM Workspace.)
- GTM Studio - The ops/marketing orchestration workspace for building automated plays and running waterfall enrichment from 25+ sources in natural language. For marketers, RevOps, and GTM engineers. Launched May 2025.
- Agent Teams - Teams of specialized AI agents that run complete GTM plays (e.g., champion activation, inbound lead routing, closed-won lookalikes) from signal to outcome, with Playbooks that set approvals and limits and a full audit trail of every action. Part of ZoomInfo's agent orchestration layer. Available in GTM Studio or headless via GTM.AI. Built on technology from ZoomInfo's acquisition of DoubleO.ai. Launched October 2026: https://pipeline.zoominfo.com/sales/zoominfo-agent-teams
- GTM.AI - Headless access to ZoomInfo data and the GTM Context Graph via API, CLI, and MCP, for developers and AI agent builders in any tool or agent: https://gtm.ai/docs/mcp
- ZoomInfo Sales - Prospecting and pipeline acceleration with verified B2B data and buying intent insights
- ZoomInfo Marketing - Account-based marketing and audience activation for demand generation teams
- ZoomInfo Operations - Data management, enrichment, and automation for revenue operations and CRM teams
- Data as a Service - ZoomInfo data delivered into customer warehouses (e.g. Snowflake), represented today by the GTM.AI lane
- Recruiting - Talent sourcing platform for finding passive candidates using real-time talent data and candidate intent signals: https://www.zoominfo.com/products/recruiting
